.Dd July 29, 2026
.Dt OPENVAS-ENTERPRISE-CONTAINER 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm openvas-enterprise-container
.Nd manage an OpenVAS Enterprise-Container deployment
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar ACTION
.Op Ar OPTIONS
.Nm
.Fl h
.Nm
.Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility initializes, configures, updates, starts, stops, and inspects an
OpenVAS Enterprise-Container deployment.
It also manages ingress certificates, feed synchronization, OCI client
credentials, and external OpenVASD scanners.
.Sh ACTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -init
Initialize the deployment, certificates, and deployment settings.
.It Fl -init-openvasd
Initialize OCI client certificates for an OpenVASD deployment.
.It Fl -change-admin-password
Change the gvmd administrator password.
.It Fl -change-feed-sync-hour
Change the scheduled feed synchronization hour.
.It Fl -force-feed-sync
Restart feed synchronization immediately.
.It Fl -update
Download the latest product version.
.It Fl -run
Start or redeploy the configured deployment.
.It Fl -logs Op Fl -service-name Ar NAME
Show deployment logs.
When
.Fl -service-name
is supplied, show logs for the named service.
.It Fl -ps
Show deployment status.
.It Fl -down
Stop the deployment.
.It Fl -down-volumes
Stop the deployment and remove volumes.
.It Fl -update-ingress-certs
Replace the ingress TLS certificate and key.
.It Fl -create-openvasd-certs
Create TLS certificates for an OpenVASD scanner.
.It Fl -create-openvasd-tar
Create an OpenVASD deployment archive.
.It Fl -get-openvasds
List OpenVASD scanners registered in gvmd.
.It Fl -add-openvasd
Register an OpenVASD scanner in gvmd.
.It Fl -del-openvasd
Remove an OpenVASD scanner from gvmd.
.El
.Sh DEPLOYMENT OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -deployment-mode Ar MODE
Set the deployment mode.
Valid values are
.Cm scan
and
.Cm openvas .
The default is
.Li ${DEPLOYMENT_MODE} .
.It Fl -feed-mode Ar MODE
Set the feed mode.
Valid values are
.Cm volume ,
.Cm service ,
and
.Cm mount .
The default is
.Li ${FEED_MODE} .
.It Fl -feed-key Ar FILE
Use
.Ar FILE
as the feed key with
.Cm volume
or
.Cm service
feed mode.
.It Fl -feed-path Ar PATH
Use
.Ar PATH
as the host feed directory with
.Cm mount
feed mode.
.It Fl -feed-sync-hour Ar HOUR
Set the scheduled feed synchronization hour.
The valid range is 1 through 24.
The default is
.Li ${GREENBONE_FEED_SYNC_JOB_HOUR} .
.It Fl -ccert-mode Ar MODE
Set the client certificate mode.
Valid values are
.Cm ca ,
.Cm cert ,
and
.Cm mount .
The default is
.Li ${CCERT_MODE} .
.It Fl -ccert-path Ar PATH
Use
.Ar PATH
as the host client certificate directory with
.Cm mount
client certificate mode.
.El
.Sh ADMINISTRATOR OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -admin-password Ar PASSWORD
Use
.Ar PASSWORD
as the administrator password during initialization or a password change.
.El
.Sh OCI CLIENT CERTIFICATE OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -license-file Ar FILE
Read the OCI registry client certificate and private key from the license file
.Ar FILE .
.It Fl -oci-client-cert Ar FILE
Use
.Ar FILE
as the OCI registry client certificate.
.It Fl -oci-client-key Ar FILE
Use
.Ar FILE
as the OCI registry client private key.
.It Fl -init-docker-oci
Install OCI credentials into dockerd using
.Xr sudo 8 .
.It Fl -skip-docker-oci
Do not install OCI credentials automatically.
Print the required commands instead.
.El
.Sh INGRESS CERTIFICATE OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -ingress-server-cert Ar FILE
Use
.Ar FILE
as the ingress server certificate.
.It Fl -ingress-server-key Ar FILE
Use
.Ar FILE
as the ingress server private key.
.El
.Sh OPENVASD OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -cn-openvasd Ar NAME
Set the OpenVASD common name and scanner hostname to
.Ar NAME .
.It Fl -openvasd-port Ar PORT
Set the OpenVASD scanner port.
The default port is 443.
.It Fl -openvasd-uuid Ar UUID
Use the scanner UUID returned by
.Fl -get-openvasds .
.It Fl -openvasd-tar-with-images
Include Docker images in the OpenVASD archive.
Disabled by default.
.It Fl -openvasd-load-images-from-tar
Load packaged Docker images before deployment.
Disabled by default.
.El
.Sh HELP OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show the help message and exit.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Initialize a scan deployment using a Docker volume for feeds:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
openvas-enterprise-container --init \\
  --oci-client-cert /path/to/product.crt \\
  --oci-client-key /path/to/product.key \\
  --feed-key /path/to/prod-feed.key
.Ed
.Pp
Initialize with a predefined administrator password:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
openvas-enterprise-container --init \\
  --admin-password 'secure-password' \\
  --oci-client-cert /path/to/product.crt \\
  --oci-client-key /path/to/product.key \\
  --feed-key /path/to/prod-feed.key
.Ed
.Pp
Initialize with scheduled feed synchronization:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
openvas-enterprise-container --init \\
  --feed-sync-hour 3 \\
  --oci-client-cert /path/to/product.crt \\
  --oci-client-key /path/to/product.key \\
  --feed-key /path/to/prod-feed.key
.Ed
.Pp
Initialize with custom ingress certificates:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
openvas-enterprise-container --init \\
  --oci-client-cert /path/to/product.crt \\
  --oci-client-key /path/to/product.key \\
  --feed-key /path/to/prod-feed.key \\
  --ingress-server-cert /path/to/ingress.crt \\
  --ingress-server-key /path/to/ingress.key
.Ed
.Pp
Update and start the deployment:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
openvas-enterprise-container --update
openvas-enterprise-container --run
.Ed
.Pp
Change the gvmd administrator password:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
openvas-enterprise-container --change-admin-password \\
  --admin-password 'new-secure-password'
.Ed
.Pp
Change the scheduled feed synchronization hour:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
openvas-enterprise-container --change-feed-sync-hour --feed-sync-hour 4
.Ed
.Pp
Restart feed synchronization immediately:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
openvas-enterprise-container --force-feed-sync
.Ed
.Pp
Show logs and status:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
openvas-enterprise-container --logs
openvas-enterprise-container --ps
.Ed
.Pp
Stop or restart the deployment:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
openvas-enterprise-container --down
openvas-enterprise-container --run
.Ed
.Pp
Stop the deployment and remove Docker volumes:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
openvas-enterprise-container --down-volumes
.Ed
.Pp
Update ingress certificates:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
openvas-enterprise-container --update-ingress-certs \\
  --ingress-server-cert ./ingress.crt \\
  --ingress-server-key ./ingress.key
.Ed
.Pp
Create OpenVASD certificates:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
openvas-enterprise-container --create-openvasd-certs \\
  --cn-openvasd sensor.example.com
.Ed
.Pp
Create an OpenVASD deployment archive:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
openvas-enterprise-container --create-openvasd-tar \\
  --cn-openvasd sensor.example.com \\
  --openvasd-tar-with-images
.Ed
.Pp
Run an extracted OpenVASD archive:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
openvas-enterprise-container --run --openvasd-load-images-from-tar
.Ed
.Pp
Run an extracted OpenVASD archive on another host port:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
openvas-enterprise-container --run \\
  --openvasd-load-images-from-tar \\
  --openvasd-port PORT
.Ed
.Pp
Register an OpenVASD scanner:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
openvas-enterprise-container --add-openvasd \\
  --cn-openvasd sensor.example.com \\
  --openvasd-port 443
.Ed
.Pp
List or remove registered OpenVASD scanners:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
openvas-enterprise-container --get-openvasds
openvas-enterprise-container --del-openvasd --openvasd-uuid UUID
.Ed
.Sh SUPPORT
Greenbone support:
.Lk https://www.greenbone.net/support/
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr less 1
